  "critical": false,
  "description": "Nuclear Electric Propulsion (NEP): a space-rated fission reactor generates 100-1000 kWe of electrical power via Brayton or Stirling conversion, which energizes ion or Hall thrusters to achieve 3000-7000 s Isp. Low thrust (mN to N) but continuous burn for weeks to years enables high delta-v cargo and science missions. Heritage: SP-100 (100 kWe), JIMO concept (100 kWe Brayton + ion). Combines reactor physics (see energy.nuclear-fission) with electric propulsion integration.",
